/// The government identifier kinds this deployment understands.
///
/// Only AADHAAR is handled in v1 — F1 §3.4 classifies it as the one identifier
/// needing ciphertext, blind index and a last-4 display form. APAAR, ABC, PEN,
/// Saral and UDISE ids are institutional identifiers designed to be shared and
/// printed; they stay plaintext on the record that owns them and never reach
/// this table.
enum GovernmentIdType {
  AADHAAR
}

/// Lifecycle of an organization's data-encryption key.
///
/// `PENDING_RECOVERY_CUSTODY` is not in F1's original set and is the honest
/// answer to an unfinished deployment: the DEK exists and works, but it has
/// only one wrap, so losing `KEK_operational` would lose the data. A key in
/// this state is refused outright in production — the application must not
/// pretend a recovery path exists when it does not.
enum DataKeyStatus {
  PENDING_RECOVERY_CUSTODY
  ACTIVE
  ROTATING
  RETIRED
  SHREDDED
}

/// The outcome a human recorded for a candidate pair.
///
/// Only DISTINCT is ever written. The opposite conclusion is not a decision
/// row — it is a merge, and merge execution is deliberately not built yet.
enum MatchDecision {
  DISTINCT
}

/// The permanent lifecycle of a learner identity.
///
/// Distinct from the applicant, admission and enrollment lifecycles: those
/// describe an attempt, a spell of study and a year's placement. This describes
/// the person's standing with the institution, and it outlives all three.
///
/// There is no `DELETED`. Leaving is a status; deletion is not a lifecycle
/// operation, and `ARCHIVED` is a write lock rather than a disappearance —
/// archived students stay searchable and reportable.
///
/// See docs/planning/student-admission-enrollment-architecture.md §19.
enum StudentStatus {
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  WITHDRAWN
  GRADUATED
  EXPELLED
  ARCHIVED
}

/// How a learner identity came into existence.
///
/// The distinction matters because it is the only thing that licenses a null
/// `sourceApplicantId`: every student born through admission has an
/// application behind them, and one that does not is a migrated record.
enum StudentCreationMode {
  ADMISSION
  MIGRATION
}
